  "intuition": "This loss applies a z-score normalization on the difference between advantages of pairs to remove scale bias and then enforces a margin using relu, encouraging a strict preference ordering with a scalable margin. It leverages advantage signals directly, making it suitable for preference optimization where the advantage gap is the primary metric.",
  "pseudocode": "advantage_diff = advantage_w - advantage_l\nnormalized_diff = zscore(advantage_diff)\nmargin = hyperparam_margin\nloss = relu(margin - normalized_diff)\nweighted_loss = loss * weight\nfinal_loss = mean(weighted_loss)",
